On the beauty side, the shelves hold imported fragrances, skincare and cosmetics, chosen for those who enjoy quality products with a European touch. The homeware range includes decorative accessories and home essentials that add character to a living space, from pieces for the table to items that finish off a shelf or bedside. The store is also a good place to look for gifts, whether for a birthday, a housewarming or a thank-you, with staff on hand to help choose and offer personal advice. Its place in Cape Quarter, among galleries, design shops and cafés, makes it an easy stop during a wander through De Waterkant. French Accent is at Cape Quarter, 27 Somerset Road, De Waterkant, Cape Town.', description_enriched_at = datetime('now') WHERE slug = 'french-accent-cape-quarter-de-waterkant' AND description = 'French Accent is an importer and retailer of luxury fragrances, beauty products and homeware in Cape Quarter, De Waterkant.' AND description_enriched_at IS NULL AND length(COALESCE(description, '')) < 700
